      ],
      "text": "Try one, right now A new blueprint question every day, with the worked answer — no account, no email, no trial. If the explanation is the standard you want, the other 2,286 are written the same way. Create a free account Browse chapter tests Question of the day 25 Aug 2026 Botany Anatomy and physiology The site of the light reaction of photosynthesis is the: A Stroma B Thylakoid membrane of the grana C Outer chloroplast membrane D Cytoplasm ANSWER B. Thylakoid membrane of the grana — Photosystems I and II are embedded in the thylakoid membranes. Pick an option to see the worked answer. A new o",
