      "type": "content",
      "x": 384,
      "y": 2733,
      "width": 1152,
      "height": 1005,
      "heading": "An AI tutor that has read your actual paper",
      "backgroundColor": "#F7F8F9",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "New An AI tutor that has read your actual paper Not a chatbot bolted on the side. It is handed the question you got wrong, the option you picked and the worked solution our subject team wrote — so it explains your mistake, and says so plainly when a question does not settle what you asked. AI tutor EXAMPLE Photo attached Why is my answer wrong? I picked B. B is what you get if you balance the atoms before the charge. That is the mistake this option was written to catch, so getting it is worth more than the mark. Manganese goes +7 in MnO₄⁻ to +2 in Mn²⁺, so the reduction half-reaction takes 5e⁻",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
